<title>GERMANY: Hoechst - has 99 pct of Roussel.</title>
<headline>Hoechst - has 99 pct of Roussel.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals giant Hoechst AG said on Tuesday that it held 99 percent of shares in French pharmaceutical company Roussel Uclaf after shareholders took up its 5.3 billion mark ($3.2 billion) offer to buy the shares.</p>
<p>Hoechst said in a statement that together with the 56.62 percent of Roussel Uclaf it already owned Hoechst now held over 99 percent of the voting shares of Roussel Uclaf.</p>
<p>&quot;As the sole shareholder of Roussel Uclaf, Hoechst has the necessary room to manoeuvre to build an integrated, global pharmaceutical company Hoechst Marion Roussel,&quot; Hoechst said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.667 German Marks)</p>
